# the SMK-37 Elite's MASTER is K1, an encoder (master.h, as main_fm1.c has it): at power-on the level is MASTER_START
# (2048, the FM-1's pot at half) and the knob the position nearest it from below (812 of 1023); a detent moves the knob
# 24 and the level follows it (the cube), so the first turn up is a step from 2048, and one back lands on 2042
wait 200
expect masterraw 812
expect master 2048
turn K1 1
expect masterraw 836
expect master 2228
turn K1 -1
expect masterraw 812
expect master 2042
# end to end in 43 detents: a spin past either end stops there; all the way down is silence (the peak is taken after
# MASTER), all the way up the cube's top (4084, the FM-1's at full)
spin K1 -40
expect masterraw 0
expect master 0
wait 200
peakreset
wait 2000
expect peak_db_max -120
spin K1 100
expect masterraw 1023
expect master 4084
peakreset
wait 2000
expect peak_db_min -20
# its position is not kept: after a power-on, MASTER_START again
spin K1 -5
reboot
wait 200
expect masterraw 812
expect master 2048
